// System Administration and Technical Tasks

// System Information
+ (system info|system information|specs|system specs)
- I'll gather system information for you. ::::: uname -a :::::

+ (uptime|how long running|system uptime)
- Checking system uptime. ::::: uptime :::::

+ (load average|system load|cpu load)
- Checking current system load. ::::: uptime :::::

+ (free memory|available memory|memory status)
- Checking memory status. ::::: free -h :::::

+ (cpu usage|processor usage|cpu status)
- Showing CPU usage information. ::::: top -n 1 :::::

// Network Operations
+ (ip address|my ip|network address)
- Getting your IP address information. ::::: ifconfig :::::

+ (network status|network info|connectivity)
- Checking network connectivity. ::::: ping -c 3 google.com :::::

+ (wifi status|wireless status)
- Checking wireless network status. ::::: iwconfig :::::

// Process Management
+ (kill process *|stop process *|end process *)
- Terminating process <star>. ::::: pkill <star> :::::

+ (kill pid *|kill process id *)
- Killing process with PID <star>. ::::: kill <star> :::::

+ (force kill *|kill 9 *)
- Force killing process <star>. ::::: kill -9 <star> :::::

+ (process list|running processes|ps)
- Listing all running processes. ::::: ps aux :::::

+ (process tree|pstree)
- Showing process tree. ::::: pstree :::::

+ (find process *|search process *)
- Searching for process <star>. ::::: ps aux | grep <star> :::::

// Package Management (macOS specific)
+ (install *|brew install *)
- Installing <star> using Homebrew. ::::: brew install <star> :::::

+ (update brew|brew update)
- Updating Homebrew package list. ::::: brew update :::::

+ (upgrade brew|brew upgrade)
- Upgrading all Homebrew packages. ::::: brew upgrade :::::

+ (search brew *|brew search *)
- Searching Homebrew for <star>. ::::: brew search <star> :::::

+ (brew list|installed packages)
- Listing installed Homebrew packages. ::::: brew list :::::

// Environment Variables
+ (show env|environment variables|env vars)
- Displaying environment variables. ::::: env :::::

+ (show path|path variable)
- Showing PATH environment variable. ::::: echo $PATH :::::

+ (set env *|export *)
- Setting environment variable. ::::: export <star> :::::

// Disk and File System
+ (disk usage|du|directory size)
- Checking disk usage. ::::: du -sh * :::::

+ (free space|available space|disk free)
- Checking available disk space. ::::: df -h :::::

+ (mount points|mounted drives)
- Showing mounted file systems. ::::: mount :::::

+ (unmount *|umount *)
- Unmounting <star>. ::::: umount <star> :::::

// Archive and Compression
+ (extract *|unzip *|decompress *)
- Extracting archive <star>. ::::: tar -xf <star> :::::

+ (create archive *|compress *|zip *)
- Creating archive from <star>. ::::: tar -czf archive.tar.gz <star> :::::

+ (list archive *|tar contents *)
- Listing contents of archive <star>. ::::: tar -tf <star> :::::

// Permissions and Ownership
+ (fix permissions *|repair permissions *)
- Fixing permissions for <star>. ::::: chmod -R 755 <star> :::::

+ (make executable *|chmod x *)
- Making <star> executable. ::::: chmod +x <star> :::::

+ (remove write *|chmod w *)
- Removing write permission from <star>. ::::: chmod -w <star> :::::

+ (show permissions *|ls l *)
- Showing detailed permissions for <star>. ::::: ls -l <star> :::::

// System Services (macOS)
+ (start service *|launchctl start *)
- Starting service <star>. ::::: sudo launchctl start <star> :::::

+ (stop service *|launchctl stop *)
- Stopping service <star>. ::::: sudo launchctl stop <star> :::::

+ (service status *|launchctl list *)
- Checking status of service <star>. ::::: launchctl list | grep <star> :::::

+ (list services|launchctl list)
- Listing all services. ::::: launchctl list :::::

// Log Management
+ (show logs|system logs|console logs)
- Showing system logs. ::::: log show --last 1h :::::

+ (error logs|show errors|system errors)
- Showing error logs. ::::: log show --predicate 'eventType == logEvent && messageType >= 16' --last 1h :::::

+ (tail syslog|follow logs)
- Following system logs. ::::: log stream :::::

+ (apache logs|web server logs)
- Showing web server logs. ::::: tail -f /var/log/apache2/error.log :::::

// Security
+ (check permissions *|security check *)
- Checking security permissions for <star>. ::::: ls -la <star> :::::

+ (show users|list users|who)
- Showing logged in users. ::::: who :::::

+ (user info *|id *)
- Showing user information for <star>. ::::: id <star> :::::

+ (change password|passwd)
- Starting password change process. ::::: passwd :::::

// System Cleanup
+ (clean cache|clear cache)
- Cleaning system cache. ::::: sudo purge :::::

+ (clean temp|clean temporary|clean tmp)
- Cleaning temporary files. ::::: rm -rf /tmp/* :::::

+ (clean downloads|empty downloads)
- Cleaning Downloads folder. ::::: rm -rf ~/Downloads/* :::::

+ (clean desktop|empty desktop)
- Cleaning Desktop. ::::: rm -rf ~/Desktop/* :::::

+ (empty trash|clean trash)
- Emptying trash. ::::: rm -rf ~/.Trash/* :::::

// Development Tools
+ (git status|check git)
- Checking git repository status. ::::: git status :::::

+ (git pull|update repo)
- Pulling latest changes from git. ::::: git pull :::::

+ (git push|push changes)
- Pushing changes to git repository. ::::: git push :::::

+ (git log|commit history)
- Showing git commit history. ::::: git log --oneline -10 :::::

+ (node version|check node)
- Checking Node.js version. ::::: node --version :::::

+ (python version|check python)
- Checking Python version. ::::: python3 --version :::::

+ (ruby version|check ruby)
- Checking Ruby version. ::::: ruby --version :::::

// Database Operations
+ (mysql start|start mysql)
- Starting MySQL server. ::::: brew services start mysql :::::

+ (mysql stop|stop mysql)
- Stopping MySQL server. ::::: brew services stop mysql :::::

+ (postgres start|start postgres)
- Starting PostgreSQL server. ::::: brew services start postgresql :::::

+ (postgres stop|stop postgres)
- Stopping PostgreSQL server. ::::: brew services stop postgresql :::::

// System Maintenance
+ (repair permissions|fix permissions)
- Running permission repair (this might take a while). ::::: sudo diskutil resetUserPermissions / `id -u` :::::

+ (rebuild spotlight|reindex spotlight)
- Rebuilding Spotlight index. ::::: sudo mdutil -E / :::::

+ (flush dns|clear dns|reset dns)
- Flushing DNS cache. ::::: sudo dscacheutil -flushcache :::::

+ (restart networking|reset network)
- Restarting network services. ::::: sudo ifconfig en0 down && sudo ifconfig en0 up :::::

// Hardware Information
+ (battery status|battery info)
- Checking battery status. ::::: pmset -g batt :::::

+ (temperature|cpu temp|system temp)
- Checking system temperature (if available). ::::: sudo powermetrics -n 1 -s smc :::::

+ (hardware info|system hardware)
- Showing hardware information. ::::: system_profiler SPHardwareDataType :::::

// Help for complex tasks
+ how do i *
- That's a great question about how to <star>. Let me help you with that step by step.

+ what is the best way to *
- There are usually several approaches to <star>. What's your specific situation?

+ troubleshoot *
- I can help troubleshoot <star>. What problems are you experiencing?

+ optimize *
- Optimizing <star> is a good idea. What aspects would you like to improve?
